+**IDEAL-W⁺ narrowing note (2026-11-16; HQ D78 correctness event; outside every registered statement span).** X4 (`:85-86`) remains a research target, not a proved theorem: X2's LS0 discovery argument is still open (CHECKPOINT.md; lemmas/L8_truth_start.md §5). This edit strengthens only the proposed delivery premises to A:IDEAL-W⁺ and does not establish P(correct report) → 1. TR1 (`Theory_work/Dept/research/FUNI_transfer/TR1_sol.md` §1–§2) identifies two shipped upper rejection predicates outside Theorem D's exit walk: `le > 1e6` (`Scripts/SMC_BVS/core/v3_run.R:96-97`, le = ℓ_n) and `cap_ll > numeric_limits<int>::max()` (`Scripts/SMC_BVS/core/cpp/v3_core.cpp:474`, cap_ll = ℓ_n + |S̃₀|). IDEAL-W excludes overflow, not these predicates. On 𝔇 := {ℓ_raw ≤ 10⁶ and ℓ_raw + ⌊n/2⌋ ≤ 2³¹ − 1}, ℓ_raw := ⌈log₂(n + p_raw + 1)⌉, both are false because ℓ_n ≤ ℓ_raw and |S̃₀| ≤ K_n ≤ ⌊n/2⌋; the exact branch reaches neither check. Under A:IDEAL-W⁺ both are false by assumption. With all stated FAC-B (C4) premises, total tier-1 fallback and allocation, including A4's P_e + A and P̄_LS0, the input/scorer and resource exclusions support the no-output step. The asymptotic target additionally requires the missing discovery proof P(𝒦_nᶜ) → 0 and the posterior expectation limit; only then does D′ give P(output and wrong) ≤ 2E[1 − π(S₀)] + P(𝒦_nᶜ) → 0 and, with delivery, P(correct report) → 1. No asymptotic conclusion follows from bounded 𝔇. The target has no every-n sentence; this note adds none. Definition (verbatim; registered assumption A:IDEAL-W⁺):
+
+**A:IDEAL-W⁺ (IDEAL-W with the two LS0 cap ceilings lifted).** IDEAL-W, exactly as defined in C-DLV `STATEMENT.md:24-25`, and the two shipped rejection predicates `le > 10⁶` (`Scripts/SMC_BVS/core/v3_run.R:96`, the LS0 base-cap validator; le = ℓ_n = ⌈log₂(n + p + 1)⌉ in the shipped configuration) and `ℓ + |S̃₀| > INT_MAX` (`Scripts/SMC_BVS/core/cpp/v3_core.cpp:474`, the disjunct `cap_ll > numeric_limits<int>::max()` of the LS0 cap-range guard, `int` read as unbounded) are false. Nothing else is lifted: the other conditions of those two validators (numeric type, length, finiteness, integrality, `le < 0`, `o.ls0_ell < 0`), every other validator, the 10⁶-maximiser start-mode enumeration cap with its tie-aware DP fallback, and every fallback and method cap are kept as coded. Like IDEAL-W and EX-A, A:IDEAL-W⁺ is an idealisation of the machine and code; a larger allocation does not imply it.
